WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.12 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Membership and subscription models

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Charge a recurring fee only where people get ongoing value worth renewing.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Define what each tier receives and why it is worth it.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Plan joining, welcome, engagement and renewal; track who leaves.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Keep paid benefits separate from voting or governance rights.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Riverside Repair Hub (Hybrid · charity with a trading company, United Kingdom)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Riverside: tool library tiers at £0 concession, £30 standard and £60 supporter, which funds one free place.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You decide whether membership fits, and design tiers if it does.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
